Negative control for the session pool's impersonation nest (parity cell P2 ·
F5 CORRECTED · H9 · AC1.3).

Removes the NESTING. Every impersonated client still renders, still carries its
expiry badge and its exit-impersonation control, and still switches the session
— they simply become flat siblings of the staff row instead of that staff
session's own group: no Collapsible, no "Impersonating" trigger, no auto-expand
on the active child, no indent rail. This is the capability the operator named
as the one the existing component had and the mock's sketch had dropped, so a
suite that cannot tell a nest from a list is not proving parity at all.

The mutant is deliberately NOT a deletion of the clients: a spec that only
asserts the impersonated client is somewhere in the pool stays GREEN under it,
which is the point — that spec was never testing P2.

